    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d927">

                <pb facs="0746" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/7866</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Simpich </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-24T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1916, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department informed [Norton] Hand under sentence death.</p>
                <p>Urgently request appropriate authorities not to execute sentence until
                    opportunity is afforded this Government for investigation.</p>
                <p>Make such investigation of case as is practicable and inform Department at
                    earliest possible date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
